// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/ui_kit.t27 -- the shared presentational kit: which of its primitives a live route
; can actually render, and which of the class names they emit any stylesheet answers
; BOUNDARY. This file owns nineteen files and nothing else: the seventeen presentational
; primitives under src/ui/components that no domain contract names -- button, card, card_media,
; modal, image_lightbox, input, loading, video_modal, video_mute, badge, chip, empty_state,
; lazy_screen, progress_bar, rarity_glow, skeleton and toast -- their module list
; src/ui/components/mod.rs, and the theme module src/ui/theme/mod.rs. About them it owns five
; facts: (1) the mount census -- which primitive a live route can render, which only has a mount
; site whose branch is never taken, and which has no live site at all; (2) the class vocabulary
; the primitives emit, which of it any rule in styles/*.css answers, and what the one host test
; over that vocabulary cannot see; (3) the render deferral LazyScreen applies; (4) the drift of the
; dead theme module against the stylesheets; (5) the media URL predicate and its hand copies. It
; owns no wording, no route, no price, no tab, no error message and no retirement: eleven sibling
; contracts own those and are named by ID below, not one of them restated.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-29 at 55a6664). None of the 46 contracts named any of these files: a scan
; of every .t27 for each file's repo-relative path found none of the nineteen, 1753 lines between
; them. They compile only for wasm32 (src/lib.rs:17-18 gates `pub mod ui`, and
; src/ui/mod.rs:12 and :15 declare components and theme), none of them carries a #[cfg(test)]
; module, and the one host instrument that reads them at all -- css_class_consistency_tests,
; src/main.rs:1609 -- reads a line only when its trimmed text starts with `class: "` and the
; quoted value holds no brace (src/main.rs:1659 and :1669). That rule sees 7 of the kit's 43 class
; attributes and none of the 67 class tokens its css_class and selected_class methods return,
; because a method returns a string and is never a `class: "` line.
; 45 of those 67 tokens have no selector in any of styles/*.css. They were not always unstyled:
; at the parent of 158500b (2026-05-15) 43 of the 45 had a rule, 37 of them in
; styles/components.css, and 158500b deleted that 852-line sheet together with its index.html
; link. docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md:421 and :458 still name the deleted sheet. All 45 sit in six
; primitives with no live mount site, so no customer is shown an unstyled one today; the one
; unstyled class that DOES render on a live route is not a method token at all: /cart mounts
; EmptyState with glass set (src/ui/screens/cart_screen.rs:197), and the glass variant adds
; card-glass (src/ui/components/empty_state.rs:22), which no rule answers.
; The census is the second finding. Counted by mount SITE, eight primitives are mounted, which is
; what the brief said. Counted by what can RENDER, six are: CardMedia's two live mounts both pass
; video_url None (src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs:859, src/ui/screens/bike_detail.rs:264; the
; bike DTO at src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs:81 carries no video field at all), so its autoplay
; branch and the mute_media_element call inside it never run on a live route; and VideoModal's
; one mount on a live screen (src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs:2378) sits inside fn ItemRow, whose
; only mount passes no video_url (src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs:1305, default None at :2315), and
; whose opener clears the Modal that contains the player in the same click (:2375, with the Modal
; opened by menu_open at :2363) while Modal renders nothing when closed
; (src/ui/components/modal.rs:43-45). Both readings are kept below, by name.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED (every claim reopened and re-measured on 2026-09-29).
; "The brief" is the task brief the round-7 ui-kit lane was handed on 2026-09-29. It is not in the
; repository, and no file in the tree carries its figures, so none of them is a source: each is kept
; below only as a refuted claim beside the measurement that refutes it, and BRIEF_IS_PUBLISHED says
; so (added 2026-09-30 at the review of round 7, which found the brief named nowhere).
;   1. "video_mute is live through CardMedia" and "video_modal is live on /admin only": each has a
;      mount site on a live screen, and neither can render -- the two paragraphs above.
;   2. "54 tokens in 7 files" is 67 in 8: the 54 leaves out skeleton's 13, which the same brief
;      then says all have rules. The 45 without a selector reproduce exactly.
;   3. "skeleton is used by lazy_screen.rs": it is not. LazyScreen draws its own inline shimmer
;      (src/ui/components/lazy_screen.rs:65-104) and mounts no Skeleton; the word matches its
;      comments at :4, :12 and :65.
;   4. "empty_state is mounted by admin_screen.rs (10 uses)": 9 mount sites plus the import at
;      src/ui/screens/admin_screen.rs:55.
;   5. "2 theme tokens differ": 2 differ as TEXT, 1 as a colour. --bg-secondary is var(--bg2) in
;      styles/variables.css:33, and --bg2 is #1a1a2e (styles/variables.css:18), the theme's value.
;   6. "the bike_card money helpers re-exported at components/mod.rs:44-46, used by 6+ screens":
;      the helpers are used, but zero uses go through that re-export; every one spells the full
;      path crate::ui::components::bike_card::.
;   7. "ChipGroup is a horizontal scroll row (:81-98)": that is its doc comment. Its class,
;      filter-tag-group (src/ui/components/chip.rs:94), has no rule, so nothing lays it out.
;   8. "The toast container sits in the top-right corner (:91)": :91 is a doc comment; the corner
;      is the rule at styles/main.css:943-945, and that rule exists.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It changes no behaviour and fixes nothing: every defect below is a
; measured, dated fact left for the owner. It decides no wording -- the kit's hard-coded copy is
; COUNTED, never quoted, and this file carries no Cyrillic -- no route (the router and the tab set
; are turbobaby/customer-surface's), no price and no dash (turbobaby/pricing-honesty's), no error
; message (turbobaby/client-errors'), no locale (turbobaby/locale-policy's) and no retirement: a
; legacy file's reach and state are turbobaby/legacy-retirement's, read through its own
; component_is_reachable and never restated as a second state machine. It picks no fate for the
; nine primitives nothing mounts and no fate for the dead theme;
; RETIREMENT_OF_UNMOUNTED_PRIMITIVES_IS_PUBLISHED says why. It names siblings by ID and
; declaration, never by line. Several sibling declarations it names (in legacy-retirement,
; availability and cart-persistence) were written the same day as this file, in the same round.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-ui-kit;

